{"name":"Arcane","hex":"#98687e","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"arcane","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Understood by only a few.","Obscure, mysterious."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arcane"}],"entries":[{"title":"Anton Arcane","blocks":[{"text":"Anton Arcane is a supervillain appearing in American comic books by DC Comics. The character first appeared in Swamp Thing #2, and was created by writer Len Wein and artist Bernie Wrightson. He is the archenemy of Swamp Thing, the protagonist of the comics."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anton_Arcane"},{"title":"Arcane (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Arcane is an animated steampunk, action-adventure television series created by Christian Linke and Alex Yee. It was produced by the French animation studio Fortiche, under the supervision of Riot Games, and distributed by Netflix. Set in Riot's League of Legends universe, it primarily focuses on sisters Violet / \"Vi\" and Powder / Jinx as they become embroiled in a conflict between their native underbelly of Zaun and the city of Piltover. First announced at the League of Legends tenth anniversary celebration in 2019, the series' first season was released in November 2021, and a second and final season was released in November 2024."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arcane_(TV_series)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a8/ArcaneNES.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a8/ArcaneNES.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Arcane as seen in the Swamp Thing video game.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArcaneNES.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Arcane_Title_Text.png/500px-Arcane_Title_Text.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","